  "title": "Aave supply DoS due to stETH 1-wei transfer discrepancy in `Distributor.supply`",
  "body": "## Finding description and impact\nWhen a user stakes stETH, the flow is:\n\n1. `DepositPool.stake()` → `Distributor.supply(depositPoolAddress, amount)`\n2. `Distributor.supply` pulls `amount` from the `DepositPool` and then calls Aave `supply` with the same `amount`.\n\nThe implementation assumes transfer-in equals `amount`. For stETH, due to the known 1 wei discrepancy on transfer, the distributor’s actual balance increases by `amount - 1`. It then instructs Aave to pull `amount`, which exceeds the distributor’s actual balance by 1 wei, so Aave’s `supply` reverts.\n\nRelevant code:\n\n```solidity\nIERC20(depositPool.token).safeTransferFrom(depositPoolAddress_, address(this), amount_);\nAaveIPool(aavePool).supply(depositPool.token, amount_, address(this), 0);\n```\n\n### Impact\n\nStaking with stETH is effectively DoS’d; transactions revert.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nTreat stETH as a fee-on-transfer/deflationary-like token pattern. Use balance delta to determine the actual received amount, then pass that to Aave.\n\n```solidity\n// before pulling\nuint256 preBalance = IERC20(depositPool.token).balanceOf(address(this));\n\n// pull from DepositPool\nIERC20(depositPool.token).safeTransferFrom(depositPoolAddress_, address(this), amount_);\n\n// compute actual received (handles stETH 1-wei discrepancy)\nuint256 received = IERC20(depositPool.token).balanceOf(address(this)) - preBalance;\nrequire(received > 0, \"No tokens received\");\n\n// supply only what was actually received\nif (depositPool.strategy == Strategy.AAVE) {\n    AaveIPool(aavePool).supply(depositPool.token, received, address(this), 0);\n}\n```"
